<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Braslav, Duke of Lower Pannonia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 884–<a href="/years/896">896</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Braslav (fl. 884–896) was the last known duke of Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a>, the Slavic principality between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drava">Drava</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a> rivers under Frankish overlordship. A loyal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the East Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnulf-of-carinthia">Arnulf of Carinthia</a>, he fought alongside him against Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, and in 896 Arnulf entrusted him with Pannonia, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zalavar">Mosaburg</a>. He disappears from the sources soon after the Hungarian conquest.</p></div>
